optimal-design and IRT test-design grounding.\"\n456\t      },\n457\t      {\n458\t        \"category\": \"architectural_shift\",\n459\t        \"query\": \"stacked generalization non-negative least squares combining predictors\",\n460\t        \"rationale\": \"Final estimator stacks candidate estimators with NNLS weights over source pseudo-target folds.\"\n461\t      },\n462\t      {\n463\t        \"category\": \"benchmark_context\",\n464\t        \"query\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v2 IFEval BBH MMLU-Pro GPQA MuSR benchmarks\",\n465\t        \"rationale\": \"Data come from per-item Open LLM Leaderboard v2 results and HELM; benchmark citations needed for dataset description.\"\n466\t      }\n467\t    ],\n468\t    \"result_driven_themes\": [\n469\t      \"Estimation error and rank correlation degrade much more for strong (out-of-range) target models than for randomly held-out targets (strong_targets MAE roughly 2x random_targets; Spearman ~0.77-0.82 vs ~0.96)\",\n470\t      \"Gains over random-subset and anchor-point baselines are small in absolute MAE terms (about 0.007-0.011) but consistent across the three variants\",\n471\t      \"Source-only validation / stacking for extrapolation to targets above the source ability range\",\n472\t      \"Posterior-mean and tail-calibration did not improve over plain logistic Fisher D-opt stacking (0.9445 vs 0.9452 combined score)\"\n473\t    ],\n474\t    \"status\": \"ready\"\n475\t  },\n476\t  \"reference_query_plans\": [\n477\t    {\n478\t      \"architectural_shifts\": [\n479\t        \"From clustering/anchor-based item selection to latent-space D-optimal selection\",\n480\t        \"From a single-model estimator to a stacked ensemble over source pseudo-target folds with incumbent fallback\",\n481\t        \"From a linear/embedding latent model to a logistic latent-ability model with upper-tail Fisher designs\"\n482\t      ],\n483\t      \"benchmarks\": [\n484\t        \"Open LLM Leaderboard v2 per-item results (IFEval, BBH, 